  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>IUPAC name of the following compound is<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/44437ce8-ff8d-4677-b034-12d505b05b2a-image.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 168px;\" /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>-Methyl-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>-oxo-hexanoic acid</p><ol>\t<li>\t<p>Identify the longest continuous carbon chain that contains the carboxyl group (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>COOH</mi></math>). In this case, it is a six-carbon chain.</p>\t</li>\t<li>\t<p>Number the carbon chain starting from the end closest to the carboxyl group. The carboxyl carbon is assigned the number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>.</p>\t</li>\t<li>\t<p>Identify and name any substituents attached to the carbon chain. In this case, there is a methyl group attached to the second carbon atom of the chain.</p>\t</li>\t<li>\t<p>Combine the substituent name with the parent chain name, with a hyphen in between. The resulting name is &quot;2-methylhexanoic acid&quot;.</p>\t</li>\t<li>\t<p>Finally, add the prefix &quot;oxo&quot; to indicate the presence of a ketone group (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>) on the fifth carbon of the chain.</p>\t</li></ol></blockquote>",
